#Cloud vs distributed systems: They use similar concepts. Distributed computing uses distributed systems by spreading tasks across many machines. It aims to create collaborative resource sharing and provide size and geographical scalability. Cloud computing, on the other hand, uses network hosted servers for storage, process, data management. It is about delivering an on demand environment using transparency, monitoring, and security.

